WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.968
- So the puzzle is why,

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.903
out of nowhere in
the last decade

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:07.340 align:start size:97% position:3%
have we seen a sudden and
sharp spike of teenage girls

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.843 align:start size:97% position:3%
who have no childhood and
history of gender dysphoria,

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.611
suddenly deciding they're trans

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.079
often with their girlfriends?

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:16.449 align:start size:84% position:16%
And the numbers
are quite alarming.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:19.619 align:start size:84% position:16%
We now have, between
2016 and 2017,

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.455
the number of young women
asking for gender surgeries

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.958
quadrupled in United States.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:28.028
(lighthearted music)

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.134 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin, and
this is The Rubin Report.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:36.903 line:0%
Joining me today for a
long overdue interview

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:40.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
is author of the new
book "Irreversible Damage

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:44.210 align:start size:88% position:13%
The Transgender Craze
Seducing Our Daughters".

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.080
Abigail Shrier, welcome
to The Rubin Report.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.948
- Thanks so much
for having me on.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.584
- So the book came out in June

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.286
and kind of caught fire in June.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:54.888
And then I was gonna
have you on in August.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.523
And I went off the grid

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:59.059 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then, you know,
there was election stuff

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.260
so I didn't have you on.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.429
And then a couple of weeks ago,

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:06.032
all hell broke loose
because Target tweeted

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:09.035
that they were gonna no
longer carry the book.

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:11.171
So let's just start
with the controversy

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.807
because actually the reason
I'm having you on right now

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:16.009
is that after the controversy,

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:18.111
the book absolutely
sold out everywhere

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.013 align:start size:81% position:19%
and we had to hold
this interview

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.448 align:start size:84% position:16%
so that the book would
be stocked again.

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:22.682
So a lot's going on.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.884 align:start size:88% position:13%
So let's just start with
the controversy first

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.853
because what you
write about here

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:30.156 align:start size:84% position:16%
in "The Transgender
Craze" is really like,

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.292
the hot topic of the day

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:33.726
and the thing that seems
to get the most people

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:34.661
in hot water.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:35.462
So what happened with Target?

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:36.696
Let's start there.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:39.032 line:0%
- Sure, so look, you
know, we're living

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.668 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
through probably the biggest
medical scandal today

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.303 line:0%
is that there's a sudden spike.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:46.172 align:start size:84% position:16%
And these teenage
girls out of nowhere,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.674
medically transitioning.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:48.942
All of a sudden they want
hormones and surgeries

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.944 align:start size:81% position:19%
and they're easily
obtaining them.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.246
And I wrote a book about it.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:56.282
And because two Twitter users

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.985
decided the book
was transphobic,

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
they told that they
called it that to Target,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.322
Target removed it.

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.823
And people were very upset.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.792
You know, the book has a
lot of grassroots support.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.862 align:start size:88% position:13%
A lot of parents feel
like it really explained

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.330
the story of what
happened to them

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.232
when they're teenagers
suddenly out of the blue,

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:14.868
decided with their friends
that they were transgender

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:17.003
and they were really upset.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.538 align:start size:84% position:16%
And a lot of people
wrote to Target

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:20.874 align:start size:84% position:16%
and Target you
know, reinstated it.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was one of the
few victories I think

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.312
against cancel culture.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.348
- Yeah you must've
been pretty enthused

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.250
to see the amount of
support that you got.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.785 align:start size:88% position:13%
Because yeah, you get
the usual Twitter haters

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.488
and the anonymous accounts
and all that stuff, you know,

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.957
pushing Target to a
decision like this.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.693
But pretty much everybody

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.829 align:start size:88% position:13%
that still stands on
the side of free speech,

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess we don't have
that many people anymore,

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.432 align:start size:88% position:13%
but pretty much
everyone that was around

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.901 align:start size:84% position:16%
supported you to
get this thing back.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.802
And it actually did work.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.337
- Yeah I was very gratified.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.474
Look, you know, there are
literally hundreds of books

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:57.443 align:start size:84% position:16%
out there promoting,
unskeptically,

00:02:57.443 --> 00:03:00.413 align:start size:88% position:13%
the immediate medical
transition of teenagers.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.248
If you want to read that book,

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.750 align:start size:81% position:19%
there are hundreds
you could read.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.418
And you know what?

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.454
I certainly would never call
for any of them to be banned

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.256
'cause I don't wanna live
in that kind of world.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.458
But you know, there
is exactly one book

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.827
that did a deep dive
into this phenomenon

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:17.063 align:start size:84% position:16%
of teenage girls
suddenly transitioning

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.531
and it's my book.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:21.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for the activists,
even one book is too many.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.603
- Yeah okay, so let's start

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.306 align:start size:84% position:16%
with the most
important question.

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:28.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's just get it out
there right from the top.

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:31.110
Abigail, are you a transphobe?

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:34.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you have an irrational
fear of trans people?

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.983
And is that why you
wrote this book?

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.651
- No, I wrote the
book first of all

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:39.752
because a reader wrote to me

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:40.853
and she told me her daughter

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.855
had gone through
this phenomenon.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.557
And when she, you know,

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.859
she said her daughter had
always been a girly girl,

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.394
never had gender dysphoria

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:51.998
this is a severe discomfort
in one's biological sex.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.433
But when she got to high school,

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.801 align:start size:84% position:16%
she had a lot of
mental health issues.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.336
And she went off to college

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:57.537
and with a group of girlfriends,

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:59.172 align:start size:84% position:16%
they all decided
they were transgender

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:02.041 align:start size:88% position:13%
and she started a
course of testosterone.

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.444
And I tried to find another
investigative journalist

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.479 align:start size:88% position:13%
who would take it up
because I had, you know,

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:08.081 align:start size:88% position:13%
I wasn't an
investigative journalist

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.549
and I couldn't find one.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:12.285 align:start size:97% position:3%
So after four months I finally
got back in touch with her

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.586
and I said all right I'll do it.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:16.122 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean that's the
world we're living in.

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:18.558
And let me just say that a
lot of transgender adults,

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:21.027
and I interviewed a lot for
my book, support the book.

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.495
I mean the book does not,

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.597 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm not against
medical transition.

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:28.601
It just urges caution when it
comes to these teenage girls.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.436
- Okay so just to
be absolutely clear

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:32.639
and I know my audience
totally understands it.

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:36.809
But so you don't have a problem
with adults that transition,

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:40.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
that make the choice in
their lives to transition?

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.582
- No, I mean not only
am I not against it,

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.517
I've interviewed a lot
of transgender adults.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:47.353 align:start size:84% position:16%
I believe it has
helped, it can help.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.889
I know them, I've
talked to them.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.324
And I'll tell you
something else,

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:54.794 align:start position:0%
I'm not even against all medical
transition for teenagers.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:57.630
The only thing I
show in the book

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.799 align:start size:84% position:16%
is that the current
medical regime

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.868 align:start size:81% position:19%
has no medical
judgment in place.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:04.704
It's totally based on the
judgment of teenagers.

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:07.573
And the doctors are told
to affirm, affirm, affirm,

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:08.841
meaning they have to agree

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:11.010 align:start size:84% position:16%
with the teenager's
self-diagnosis.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.979
So there's no checks in place.

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:14.580 align:start size:84% position:16%
So the regime, the
current medical regime

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.883
is really not safe
for teenage girls.

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.117
- Yeah, so I was trying to think

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.353 align:start size:84% position:16%
how I wanted to
conduct this interview

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:22.555
because, you know, this
is one of the topics

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:24.057
that we've touched
on a bunch here.

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:28.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not because I particularly
care about these issues

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:30.897 align:start size:97% position:3%
as much as when it's become
such a hot button issue

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:32.231
then it sort of
gets to my plate.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.666 align:start size:81% position:19%
But I thought,
I've read the book

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.769
and I thought that the
way that you laid it out

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.204
just even in the chapters,

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:40.673 align:start size:97% position:3%
the way you separated certain
things was really good.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:41.874
So if you don't mind,

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:42.909
we'll just go through
chapter by chapter

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:44.577
and discuss each one.

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:47.113
So the introduction is
about the contagion.

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:48.648 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's sort of
what you're hitting on

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:51.250
about what happened with your
friend's daughter at college.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.119
Can you describe that?

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:56.422
- Sure so it's based on the
research of Lisa Littman

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:57.490
as we'll talk about
in the next chapter.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.425
But the public health researcher

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:01.394
who looked into why
there was a sudden

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:03.596
and huge spike in teenage girls

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:05.898
who claimed to have
gender dysphoria.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:08.868 align:start size:97% position:3%
And this is not the population
that traditionally had it,

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.536
it was always males.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.739
And it usually began
in early childhood.

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:15.808
And all of a sudden across
the West, including America,

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:18.811 align:start size:84% position:16%
we have this sudden
spike of teenage girls

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.113
deciding they're transgender,

00:06:20.113 --> 00:06:21.547
often with their friends

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:23.483
and often after
the encouragement

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:25.518
of social media influencers.

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:28.221
- Right so you talk about this

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.522
a little bit later in the book.

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:30.456
So I'm jumping ahead a bit.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.291
But you tell a story of a girl

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:35.628 align:start size:97% position:3%
who in essence in high school
came out as transgender.

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:37.397
There weren't a lot of issues

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:38.831 align:start size:84% position:16%
that she was bringing
up before that,

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:42.068 align:start size:97% position:3%
but then suddenly she's
getting more likes on Tumblr.

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:44.804 align:start size:97% position:3%
She's now part of an
oppressed minority at school

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:45.838
and in different groups.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:48.341
And that that allure basically,

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:49.842 align:start position:0%
and I know I'm getting a
little ahead of ourselves here,

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:52.478
but that allure, in a weird way,

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:55.014
is what's fueling
so much of this.

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:55.948
- That's right.

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:57.450
So it's young teenage girls.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.819
These are often white, middle
or upper middle class girls.

00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:01.687
They're very precocious

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:04.857
but they are high-anxiety
and high-depression girls.

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:06.926
They have a lot of
mental health issues.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.394
And for the first time,

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:10.763 align:start size:97% position:3%
the moment they get to high
school or middle school

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:13.166 align:start size:84% position:16%
and decide they're
transgender, you know,

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:15.701
it's the first time they
get so much encouragement

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:18.304
and love, especially online.

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:19.939
And sometimes from adults.

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:24.944 align:start size:97% position:3%
And some of these adults are
not up to very much good.

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:27.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they get the showering
of love and praise

00:07:27.547 --> 00:07:29.949
and they don't wanna
walk away from that.

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:32.084 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So chapter one which
is about the girls

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you're
describing right there

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:34.854 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, we've
talked a lot about.

00:07:34.854 --> 00:07:36.823
And I think you know I was
on tour with Jordan Peterson

00:07:36.823 --> 00:07:38.090
for a year and a half.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:41.260
And he focused more so I
would say on young men,

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it was a message
that obviously traversed,

00:07:43.663 --> 00:07:45.698
it didn't matter what
gender you really were.

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:50.002 align:start position:0%
But is there something specific
going on with young girls

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:51.504
that we're not aware of?

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:54.307
Like there does seem to be an
emasculization of young boys

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:55.775
that we see.

00:07:55.775 --> 00:07:57.677
But what do you think is
happening with young girls?

00:07:57.677 --> 00:08:00.046
- Right, so teenage
girls specifically

00:08:00.046 --> 00:08:02.815
fall for almost every one of
these so-called hysterias.

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:04.350
And the reason they do

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:07.019
is they tend to take
on their friend's pain.

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:08.788
If a young man is depressed,

00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:12.525
very often his friend will say
okay let's go play basketball

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:14.927
or suggest doing something.

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:17.196 align:start size:84% position:16%
But he won't say,
what are you feeling?

00:08:17.196 --> 00:08:18.764
Tell me about your pain.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:20.967
And he won't start to
take it on himself.

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:24.871 align:start size:97% position:3%
He won't agree with his friend
about how terrible life is

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:26.672
just to make his
friend feel better.

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:28.207
But we know,

00:08:28.207 --> 00:08:29.742
and I interviewed a lot of
psychologists about this,

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:32.078
young women tend to not only
take on their friend's pain

00:08:32.078 --> 00:08:34.113 align:start size:81% position:19%
they're willing
to distort reality

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:36.749 align:start size:84% position:16%
in order to make their
friend feel better.

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:39.051 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so that's why they
tend to, you know,

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:42.688 align:start size:97% position:3%
all of these, you know,
anorexia is spread this way.

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:46.893
They tend to take on whatever
their friend's reality is.

00:08:46.893 --> 00:08:48.961
Even if it's oh, I'm too fat.

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:51.397 align:start size:97% position:3%
Whatever they think will make
their friend feel better,

00:08:51.397 --> 00:08:52.598
they'll take that on.

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:54.066
- Do you get pushback

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:56.636
when even you talk about
something sort of as simple

00:08:56.636 --> 00:08:57.770
and kind of obvious?

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.205
Like we all know that is true,

00:08:59.205 --> 00:09:00.540
men care more about things,

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:01.741
women care more about people.

00:09:01.741 --> 00:09:03.342 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like these are things
that we all know.

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:05.444 align:start size:84% position:16%
But even saying
something like that,

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:06.946
do you find that
you get pushback

00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:08.414
from the scientific
community on that?

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:10.850
That just boys and girls are
wired a little bit differently?

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:13.553
And of course there's
exceptions to the rule.

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:16.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
But as a general rule what
you just said is true.

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:19.492
- Right, so I do
get some pushback.

00:09:19.492 --> 00:09:20.927
But actually I get
a lot of, you know,

00:09:20.927 --> 00:09:22.328 align:start size:84% position:16%
I interviewed a lot
of people for the book

00:09:22.328 --> 00:09:24.463 align:start position:0%
and a lot of scientific experts
and a lot of them agree.

00:09:24.463 --> 00:09:27.967
I mean we know that you
can't house young women

00:09:27.967 --> 00:09:30.336
who are anorexic on a
hospital wards together

00:09:30.336 --> 00:09:31.571
without being really careful.

00:09:31.571 --> 00:09:33.773
Because they will tend
to encourage each other

00:09:33.773 --> 00:09:36.375
and their anorexia
will get more severe.

00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:37.810
And it's, we don't...

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:40.012
It's not comparable with boys.

00:09:40.012 --> 00:09:42.214
They don't go through
quite the same things.

00:09:43.349 --> 00:09:45.251
- So chapter two is the puzzle.

00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:46.786
Let's talk about the puzzle.

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:49.322
- So the puzzle is why,

00:09:49.322 --> 00:09:51.424
out of nowhere in
the last decade,

00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:54.894 align:start size:97% position:3%
have we seen a sudden and
sharp spike of teenage girls

00:09:54.894 --> 00:09:57.396 align:start size:97% position:3%
who have no childhood and
history of gender dysphoria,

00:09:57.396 --> 00:09:59.165
suddenly deciding they're trans

00:09:59.165 --> 00:10:00.666
often with their girlfriends?

00:10:00.666 --> 00:10:04.003 align:start size:84% position:16%
And the numbers
are quite alarming.

00:10:04.003 --> 00:10:07.173
We now have, you know,
between 2016 and 2017

00:10:07.173 --> 00:10:10.009
the number of young women
asking for gender surgeries

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:12.244
quadrupled in United States.

00:10:13.646 --> 00:10:16.148 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
And we know it's
typically teenage girls

00:10:16.148 --> 00:10:20.219 line:0%
who are driving this population.

00:10:20.219 --> 00:10:21.821
So the question is, why?

00:10:21.821 --> 00:10:23.556
What is it about teenage girls?

00:10:23.556 --> 00:10:26.859
Whenever you have any kind of

00:10:26.859 --> 00:10:29.128
you know, diagnosis
that's exploding,

00:10:29.128 --> 00:10:32.999 align:start size:84% position:16%
it really is
important to ask why.

00:10:32.999 --> 00:10:34.867 align:start size:84% position:16%
And, you know, we're
not seeing this

00:10:34.867 --> 00:10:36.869
with women in their 60s and 70s,

00:10:36.869 --> 00:10:38.704
we're seeing the same population

00:10:38.704 --> 00:10:41.474
that falls for every
other peer contagion.

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:44.377
- So what would you say the,

00:10:44.377 --> 00:10:46.112
well you get to this
a little bit later,

00:10:46.112 --> 00:10:47.279
but what would you say

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:50.282 align:start size:84% position:16%
is sort of the
answer to the puzzle?

00:10:50.282 --> 00:10:51.684
I mean is it...

00:10:51.684 --> 00:10:53.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or it's just a confluence
of many things,

00:10:53.619 --> 00:10:56.389
education, social media
and everything, right?

00:10:56.389 --> 00:10:57.690
- Right, and young women

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:59.659
who are in genuine
psychological pain

00:10:59.659 --> 00:11:01.127
and these women are,

00:11:01.127 --> 00:11:03.629 align:start position:0%
they tend to look to the culture
to help them understand it.

00:11:03.629 --> 00:11:05.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
So in previous generations
they might've said,

00:11:05.097 --> 00:11:06.666 align:start size:84% position:16%
oh, I'm so fat,
that's the problem.

00:11:06.666 --> 00:11:08.634 align:start size:88% position:13%
If I just lose this
weight I'll feel better.

00:11:08.634 --> 00:11:10.536
And today they look in
their culture and say,

00:11:10.536 --> 00:11:11.704
oh, I know what this is.

00:11:11.704 --> 00:11:13.472
I don't feel perfectly feminine.

00:11:13.472 --> 00:11:15.408
I'm 13, I hate my body.

00:11:15.408 --> 00:11:16.942
I must have gender dysphoria.

00:11:16.942 --> 00:11:18.778
I'm supposed to be a boy.

00:11:18.778 --> 00:11:20.479
- Yeah and that's one of
the hardest things there.

00:11:20.479 --> 00:11:23.916 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because you have girls
that have legitimate issues

00:11:23.916 --> 00:11:25.151
that they need to deal with

00:11:25.151 --> 00:11:28.287 align:start size:88% position:13%
that adults should be
there to deal with them.

00:11:28.287 --> 00:11:31.824 align:start size:97% position:3%
And yet they're being
prescribed the wrong thing.

00:11:31.824 --> 00:11:34.226 align:start size:88% position:13%
- You might even say
that's the entire issue.

00:11:34.226 --> 00:11:37.763 align:start size:97% position:3%
The entire issue is really,
and here's the problem,

00:11:37.763 --> 00:11:40.633 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's not that transition
is never appropriate.

00:11:40.633 --> 00:11:44.770
But we are living with this
affirmative care model now.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:47.506 align:start size:97% position:3%
Which means that across
the West, doctors are told,

00:11:47.506 --> 00:11:50.910 align:start size:97% position:3%
with this diagnosis, you
must agree with the patient,

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:52.211
no matter how young she is

00:11:52.211 --> 00:11:54.080
or what are her other
mental health issues.

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:56.682
When she self-diagnoses
with gender dysphoria,

00:11:56.682 --> 00:11:57.850
you agree with her.

00:11:57.850 --> 00:11:59.118 align:start size:84% position:16%
And your next
question is basically,

00:11:59.118 --> 00:12:01.420
when do we start the medication?

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.355
There's no oversight.

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:06.726 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, so it's an interesting
segue to the influencers,

00:12:06.726 --> 00:12:08.194
which is the next chapter.

00:12:08.194 --> 00:12:10.796 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm really fascinated by this,
on how this stuff spreads.

00:12:12.231 --> 00:12:15.134
- Yeah, so there are a lot
of social media influencers.

00:12:15.134 --> 00:12:20.139
And for Gen Z, those
born in 1995 and after,

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:23.709 align:start size:88% position:13%
social media influencers
are as important,

00:12:23.709 --> 00:12:26.312
if not more important
than Hollywood stars..

00:12:26.312 --> 00:12:28.948 align:start size:97% position:3%
They really follow these
people, they look up to them.

00:12:28.948 --> 00:12:31.584
And unfortunately there are
a lot of trans influencers

00:12:31.584 --> 00:12:34.053 align:start size:84% position:16%
who are pedaling very,
very bad messages.

00:12:34.053 --> 00:12:36.155
Like transition is easy.

00:12:36.155 --> 00:12:37.690 align:start size:84% position:16%
Even if you don't
know if you're trans,

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.259 align:start size:84% position:16%
you should try a
course of testosterone

00:12:40.259 --> 00:12:42.161 align:start size:84% position:16%
'cause that's the
only way to find out

00:12:42.161 --> 00:12:43.429
if you're the real thing.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.832
And they really downplay
the medical side effects

00:12:46.832 --> 00:12:49.535 align:start size:88% position:13%
which are really severe
and irreversible.

00:12:49.535 --> 00:12:52.438
- So what do you make of
the click part of this?

00:12:52.438 --> 00:12:54.273
The people that are influencers

00:12:54.273 --> 00:12:55.808
that keep talking
about this stuff,

00:12:55.808 --> 00:12:57.276 align:start size:88% position:13%
even if they don't
understand the science,

00:12:57.276 --> 00:12:59.678 align:start size:88% position:13%
even if they themselves
are not trans.

00:12:59.678 --> 00:13:01.080
But that, for some reason,

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:04.583 align:start size:97% position:3%
there seems to be a tremendous
amount of just clicks.

00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:07.253 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, literally just
clicks and eyeballs

00:13:07.253 --> 00:13:08.954
that seem to drive this.

00:13:08.954 --> 00:13:11.223
- Right, so one thing is,

00:13:11.223 --> 00:13:13.526
you know I interviewed
influencers for my book.

00:13:13.526 --> 00:13:17.129 align:start position:0%
And I do think some of them
really believe they're helping.

00:13:17.129 --> 00:13:18.831
And one of the reasons they...

00:13:18.831 --> 00:13:22.168 align:start position:0%
And they do genuinely feel
great about having transitioned.

00:13:22.168 --> 00:13:24.069
And one of the reasons they do

00:13:24.069 --> 00:13:27.106 align:start size:88% position:13%
is because testosterone
delivers a euphoria

00:13:27.106 --> 00:13:28.841
and it suppresses anxiety,

00:13:28.841 --> 00:13:31.143
which is some of these
girls' biggest problems.

00:13:31.143 --> 00:13:34.480
So they go on it and they
think it's confirmation

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:36.816
that they got their
diagnosis right.

00:13:36.816 --> 00:13:38.117
And they feel great

00:13:38.117 --> 00:13:40.553 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they can't wait
to tell their friends.

00:13:40.553 --> 00:13:43.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
The problem is we're
already seeing long-term,

00:13:43.222 --> 00:13:45.324
you know, when you step out
of even just a few years,

00:13:45.324 --> 00:13:47.259
there's tremendous
rates of regret,

00:13:47.259 --> 00:13:49.595
and there's tremendous rates
of anxiety and depression.

00:13:49.595 --> 00:13:52.731 align:start size:97% position:3%
It is not curing depression
in many instances.

00:13:52.731 --> 00:13:55.901
And there really was no
medical oversight for it.

00:13:55.901 --> 00:13:57.169 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Yeah and there's
really nothing

00:13:57.169 --> 00:13:59.104
that can be done
about that, right?

00:13:59.104 --> 00:14:01.407
I mean about the
influencers that,

00:14:01.407 --> 00:14:03.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
for either good intentions
or bad intentions,

00:14:03.609 --> 00:14:05.778
I mean, it is what it
is, we're all online.

00:14:06.812 --> 00:14:08.180
- Yeah, I mean, you know,

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:10.516
getting some of these
young girls offline

00:14:10.516 --> 00:14:11.650
is a good first step.

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:13.219
Look, when there was lots of,

00:14:13.219 --> 00:14:14.920
I think they called it thinspo,

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:16.388
you know, the thinspiration on,

00:14:16.388 --> 00:14:19.425
I think it was Instagram or one
of these social media sites,

00:14:19.425 --> 00:14:20.693
they took it down

00:14:20.693 --> 00:14:24.163
because inspiring girls
to anorexia was harmful.

00:14:24.163 --> 00:14:27.066
But right now we have
trans influencers,

00:14:27.066 --> 00:14:29.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
people who are suggesting
and encouraging

00:14:29.468 --> 00:14:31.503 align:start size:84% position:16%
taking testosterone,
trying it out,

00:14:31.503 --> 00:14:34.907
seeing how it feels
basically online.

00:14:34.907 --> 00:14:36.075
And it's basically a Wild West.

00:14:36.075 --> 00:14:38.878 align:start size:88% position:13%
They're never shut
down because, you know,

00:14:38.878 --> 00:14:41.547
whenever someone says it's
a matter of civil rights

00:14:41.547 --> 00:14:44.617 align:start size:88% position:13%
or a minority, everyone
stops thinking.

00:14:44.617 --> 00:14:48.287
And certainly social media
doesn't police that at all.

00:14:48.287 --> 00:14:49.889
- How long do they,

00:14:49.889 --> 00:14:51.423
when people start taking,

00:14:51.423 --> 00:14:53.325
or when these young girls
start taking testosterone,

00:14:53.325 --> 00:14:56.562 align:start size:97% position:3%
how long does that bump that
you described there last,

00:14:56.562 --> 00:14:58.731
where the anxiety
is gonna go down

00:14:58.731 --> 00:15:00.799
and that sense of euphoria?

00:15:00.799 --> 00:15:03.903
- I've talked to trans adults

00:15:03.903 --> 00:15:05.871 align:start size:84% position:16%
who've said it lasted
their whole life.

00:15:05.871 --> 00:15:09.808 align:start size:97% position:3%
In other words, they really
felt that in their case

00:15:09.808 --> 00:15:13.779
that testosterone was
a really helpful drug.

00:15:15.781 --> 00:15:17.383
And I'm fine with that.

00:15:17.383 --> 00:15:19.051
The only problem, of course,

00:15:19.051 --> 00:15:21.220
is that in the trans
adults I talked to,

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:25.291 align:start size:88% position:13%
they had to have certain
therapy to make sure.

00:15:25.291 --> 00:15:26.525
And there was oversight

00:15:26.525 --> 00:15:28.527 align:start size:84% position:16%
to make sure it was
the correct diagnosis.

00:15:28.527 --> 00:15:29.929
Because right now,

00:15:29.929 --> 00:15:32.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
teenage girls are deciding
this on their own.

00:15:32.164 --> 00:15:35.734 align:start size:88% position:13%
And there isn't a
mental health oversight

00:15:35.734 --> 00:15:37.970
in any meaningful way.

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:39.238
- Right, so we'll get more

00:15:39.238 --> 00:15:41.307
to the medical part of
that in a little bit.

00:15:41.307 --> 00:15:43.142
But so chapter five
is about the schools.

00:15:43.142 --> 00:15:45.044
And I think this is
kind of fascinating

00:15:45.044 --> 00:15:48.314
because we've sort of just
watched intellectual rot

00:15:48.314 --> 00:15:50.816
run across all of our schools.

00:15:50.816 --> 00:15:52.351
And you just have to kind of go

00:15:52.351 --> 00:15:56.121 align:start size:84% position:16%
with whatever the
thing of the day is.

00:15:57.389 --> 00:15:59.425 align:start size:88% position:13%
How much of this is just
sort of being taught

00:15:59.425 --> 00:16:00.759
at public schools, do you think?

00:16:00.759 --> 00:16:02.127 align:start size:84% position:16%
I know it depends
what state you're in,

00:16:02.127 --> 00:16:04.330
but here we are both in Cali.

00:16:05.497 --> 00:16:07.266 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So in California-
- For better or worse.

00:16:07.266 --> 00:16:10.202 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right, it's very
extreme in this state.

00:16:10.202 --> 00:16:12.504
So gender identity education

00:16:12.504 --> 00:16:14.039
is something you
can't opt out of.

00:16:14.039 --> 00:16:16.575
It begins in kindergarten
and it's really extreme.

00:16:16.575 --> 00:16:19.945
We start by teaching
five-year-olds that,

00:16:19.945 --> 00:16:21.046
however they were born,

00:16:21.046 --> 00:16:22.448
a doctor just made a guess

00:16:22.448 --> 00:16:24.650
and only they know
their true gender.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:29.521
And this doesn't push kids
to transition necessarily.

00:16:29.521 --> 00:16:31.390
But what it does
do is the moment

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:34.326 align:start size:97% position:3%
these young girls in
particular hit adolescence,

00:16:34.326 --> 00:16:36.462 align:start size:97% position:3%
they go through a period where
they hate their own bodies.

00:16:36.462 --> 00:16:37.963
They feel ugly.

00:16:37.963 --> 00:16:40.232
This is something nearly
every woman can attest to.

00:16:41.333 --> 00:16:43.969 align:start size:84% position:16%
The solution readily
leaps to mind

00:16:43.969 --> 00:16:45.938 align:start size:97% position:3%
because it's something they've
learned about for years.

00:16:45.938 --> 00:16:47.873
And it's that, oh my gosh,

00:16:47.873 --> 00:16:50.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know why I'm so
uncomfortable in my body.

00:16:50.275 --> 00:16:52.311 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's 'cause I'm
supposed to be a boy.

00:16:52.311 --> 00:16:53.879
- Were you able to
figure out at all,

00:16:53.879 --> 00:16:58.884 align:start position:0%
how these bad ideas get so
influential at all the schools?

00:17:00.319 --> 00:17:01.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
Seemingly all the schools,
at least in California.

00:17:01.687 --> 00:17:04.056
But New York too, and
all over the country.

00:17:04.056 --> 00:17:06.525 align:start size:84% position:16%
Just how infectious
the ideas are.

00:17:06.525 --> 00:17:07.793
- Right, so I was, a little bit.

00:17:07.793 --> 00:17:09.862
Because I was able to
get a lot of documents

00:17:09.862 --> 00:17:11.997
out of the California
Teachers Association.

00:17:11.997 --> 00:17:15.067
Concerned teachers
sent them to be,

00:17:15.067 --> 00:17:16.335
uh, sent them to me.

00:17:16.335 --> 00:17:20.205
And there's really no
division in California

00:17:20.205 --> 00:17:22.841 align:start size:84% position:16%
between the activists
and the teachers.

00:17:22.841 --> 00:17:25.344
Activists are not only
training the teachers,

00:17:25.344 --> 00:17:28.347
they are providing
all the curriculum

00:17:28.347 --> 00:17:33.052 align:start size:97% position:3%
for gender identity and
sexual orientation education.

00:17:33.052 --> 00:17:35.854
So it's coming from
very extreme sources.

00:17:35.854 --> 00:17:38.724 align:start size:97% position:3%
And in teachers who are a
little uncomfortable about it

00:17:38.724 --> 00:17:42.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
are completely
intimidated into silence.

00:17:42.061 --> 00:17:44.029 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So when you say that
at five years old,

00:17:44.029 --> 00:17:45.697
they're taught this,

00:17:46.865 --> 00:17:48.100
for the average parent

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:49.802
that might go into
that school and say,

00:17:49.802 --> 00:17:51.970 align:start position:0%
well, I don't want my child
hearing that at five years old.

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:53.472
Which no five-year-old,

00:17:53.472 --> 00:17:54.873
it has nothing to do with
even what's true or not,

00:17:54.873 --> 00:17:57.709
no five-year-old can
comprehend this stuff.

00:17:57.709 --> 00:18:00.446
In effect, that person
is gonna be blacklisted

00:18:00.446 --> 00:18:03.515 align:start size:97% position:3%
and God only knows what
they'll do to the poor kid.

00:18:03.515 --> 00:18:05.617
- That's right, you can't.

00:18:05.617 --> 00:18:08.387
Because in California, they
did something really sneaky.

00:18:08.387 --> 00:18:12.858
They put this curriculum into
the anti-bullying curriculum.

00:18:12.858 --> 00:18:14.293
So usually you would think

00:18:14.293 --> 00:18:16.128 align:start size:84% position:16%
this would go into
the sex ed curriculum,

00:18:16.128 --> 00:18:18.564 align:start size:84% position:16%
which parents are
allowed to opt out of.

00:18:18.564 --> 00:18:20.799
But they put it into the
anti-bullying curriculum

00:18:20.799 --> 00:18:21.967
under the pretext

00:18:21.967 --> 00:18:24.002 align:start size:88% position:13%
that you couldn't
possibly police bullying

00:18:24.002 --> 00:18:25.971
unless you taught every child

00:18:25.971 --> 00:18:28.240
that only they know
their true gender.

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:30.375 align:start size:84% position:16%
And of course we
know that's nonsense

00:18:30.375 --> 00:18:32.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you can
absolutely police bullying

00:18:32.744 --> 00:18:34.279
and should police bullying

00:18:34.279 --> 00:18:37.216
against sexual minorities
and every other student,

00:18:37.216 --> 00:18:42.221 align:start size:97% position:3%
without introducing everybody
to a false ideology.

00:18:43.088 --> 00:18:44.556
- Yeah, do you have any numbers

00:18:44.556 --> 00:18:46.725
on what percentage of the
public school teachers

00:18:46.725 --> 00:18:49.528
actually buy it verse
who's just going along?

00:18:49.528 --> 00:18:51.597
I guess that would
be hard to quantify.

00:18:51.597 --> 00:18:52.731
- It's very hard.

00:18:52.731 --> 00:18:54.333 align:start size:84% position:16%
Public school teachers
are terrified.

