00:28:40.485 --> 00:28:43.755 align:start size:88% position:13%
that this is seems to
be innate and immutable.

00:28:43.755 --> 00:28:45.790
It's not the kind
of thing you can

00:28:45.790 --> 00:28:48.860
sort of convert someone out
of or convince them out of.

00:28:48.860 --> 00:28:50.995
And nor should you want to.

00:28:50.995 --> 00:28:55.133 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, there's nothing
unhealthy about a gay life.

00:28:55.133 --> 00:28:56.601
There just isn't.

00:28:56.601 --> 00:28:58.903
But when you're talking about

00:28:58.903 --> 00:29:02.474 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, letting a
child be uncomfortable

00:29:02.474 --> 00:29:04.008
in their own body.

00:29:04.008 --> 00:29:06.411
Because gender identity, if
a young woman suddenly says,

00:29:06.411 --> 00:29:08.613
I'm really a boy, I
need to become a boy,

00:29:08.613 --> 00:29:11.750
you're setting them up to be
a lifetime medical patient

00:29:11.750 --> 00:29:13.752 align:start size:97% position:3%
where they will put
testosterone in their bodies.

00:29:13.752 --> 00:29:15.553
They need to stay
on it for life.

00:29:15.553 --> 00:29:19.357 align:start size:97% position:3%
It has all kinds of terribly
extreme side effects.

00:29:19.357 --> 00:29:21.559
They're highly risky.

00:29:21.559 --> 00:29:24.596
And unlike, you know, therapy

00:29:24.596 --> 00:29:27.198 align:start size:88% position:13%
that may make her
comfortable in her body,

00:29:27.198 --> 00:29:31.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
the today's therapy
pushes her to transition.

00:29:31.069 --> 00:29:34.005 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's very different
from being gay

00:29:34.005 --> 00:29:35.774
in which all the gay person asks

00:29:35.774 --> 00:29:38.409 align:start size:88% position:13%
is that you accept
them for what they are.

00:29:39.477 --> 00:29:41.045
What a trans teen asks is,

00:29:41.045 --> 00:29:43.214
can you help me try
to be what I'm not?

00:29:43.214 --> 00:29:46.751
And that's a much more
invasive intervention.

00:29:46.751 --> 00:29:49.087
- Yeah, you know, I'm reminded
as you're talking about this,

00:29:49.087 --> 00:29:51.389 align:start position:0%
I'm blanking on whether you
mentioned this show in the book.

00:29:51.389 --> 00:29:53.491 align:start size:97% position:3%
Did you talk about
"Transparent" at all the show?

00:29:53.491 --> 00:29:54.959
- No, I didn't.

00:29:54.959 --> 00:29:59.297 align:start position:0%
- So there's a line in the last
episode of the first season

00:29:59.297 --> 00:30:02.000
where a woman who's
already transitioned

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:05.470 align:start position:0%
says to the main character who's
about to begin the process,

00:30:05.470 --> 00:30:07.639
in effect, this is
gonna ruin your life.

00:30:07.639 --> 00:30:08.973
This is gonna ruin your family.

00:30:08.973 --> 00:30:10.141
And that, in many ways,

00:30:10.141 --> 00:30:12.977 align:start size:84% position:16%
is what the show
ended up being about.

00:30:12.977 --> 00:30:15.547 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I know that's not about
a child transitioning,

00:30:15.547 --> 00:30:17.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I think a lot of
what you're talking about

00:30:17.015 --> 00:30:18.383
is just that so many people

00:30:18.383 --> 00:30:20.518
just don't have a holistic view

00:30:20.518 --> 00:30:24.122
of what this is going to
be like on the other side.

00:30:24.122 --> 00:30:25.323
- That's exactly right.

00:30:25.323 --> 00:30:27.091 align:start size:84% position:16%
And when I interviewed
transgender adults

00:30:27.091 --> 00:30:30.728 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
who are very happy in their
transitions very often,

00:30:30.728 --> 00:30:31.830 line:0%
they will still tell me,

00:30:31.830 --> 00:30:33.464 line:0%
look, this is not easy.

00:30:33.464 --> 00:30:35.533 line:0%
It's not easy to go through life

00:30:35.533 --> 00:30:37.435
on all this hormonal treatment.

00:30:37.435 --> 00:30:39.337
You know, holding yourself out

00:30:39.337 --> 00:30:40.805
as a member of the opposite sex,

00:30:40.805 --> 00:30:42.240
it's really hard.

00:30:42.240 --> 00:30:44.442 align:start size:97% position:3%
And when transgender
adults talk to me about it,

00:30:44.442 --> 00:30:46.144 align:start size:81% position:19%
they are horrified
that teenagers

00:30:46.144 --> 00:30:49.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
are getting this hormonal
treatments so easily,

00:30:49.948 --> 00:30:52.684 align:start size:97% position:3%
without any kind of
understanding of the risks,

00:30:54.185 --> 00:30:58.156
and not appreciating how hard
medical transition really is.

00:30:58.156 --> 00:30:59.490
- So all that being said,

00:30:59.490 --> 00:31:02.093 align:start size:84% position:16%
chapter seven is
about the dissidents.

00:31:02.093 --> 00:31:04.462 align:start size:88% position:13%
There are some
dissidents in the field.

00:31:05.330 --> 00:31:06.798
- That's right.

00:31:06.798 --> 00:31:08.266 align:start size:97% position:3%
A number of prominent people
have stood out and said,

00:31:08.266 --> 00:31:10.101
hold on, this is way too much,

00:31:10.101 --> 00:31:12.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
way too fast with too
little medical oversight.

00:31:13.738 --> 00:31:15.840 align:start size:81% position:19%
You know, look,
the court found...

00:31:15.840 --> 00:31:17.175
And I interviewed a lot of them,

00:31:17.175 --> 00:31:20.511
including Ken Zucker
who chaired the entry,

00:31:20.511 --> 00:31:23.047 align:start size:88% position:13%
the writing of the entry
on gender dysphoria

00:31:23.047 --> 00:31:26.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the DSM-5, the
classic psychiatric manual

00:31:27.719 --> 00:31:29.120
on mental disorders.

00:31:29.120 --> 00:31:32.323
And these are people who say,

00:31:32.323 --> 00:31:36.294 align:start size:97% position:3%
starting with the conclusion
is not medicine, right?

00:31:36.294 --> 00:31:38.563
And in fact, last week,

00:31:38.563 --> 00:31:41.799 align:start size:97% position:3%
the British high court
examined the same protocols

00:31:41.799 --> 00:31:44.202
that they have in place in
Britain for gender medicine.

00:31:44.202 --> 00:31:46.304
And the high court was appalled.

00:31:46.304 --> 00:31:49.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said, in effect,
what's been going on here

00:31:49.674 --> 00:31:52.810
is likely to transition
a lot of young women

00:31:52.810 --> 00:31:55.480
who are not supposed
to be transgender.

00:31:55.480 --> 00:31:56.948
And a lot of young people

00:31:56.948 --> 00:31:59.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are likely to
experience severe regret.

00:31:59.884 --> 00:32:02.887
- So are you surprised,

00:32:02.887 --> 00:32:04.722 align:start size:97% position:3%
I guess this is the right
chapter to ask you about this,

00:32:04.722 --> 00:32:09.594 align:start position:0%
are you surprised how this thing
so part of the culture war.

00:32:09.594 --> 00:32:11.095
That it's not just,

00:32:11.095 --> 00:32:13.698
okay, this is happening
to young girls at school,

00:32:13.698 --> 00:32:14.699
that's one portion of it,

00:32:14.699 --> 00:32:16.467
but this is becoming something

00:32:18.069 --> 00:32:19.337
that Joe Biden is tweeting

00:32:19.337 --> 00:32:21.406 align:start size:84% position:16%
about transgender
violence all the time.

00:32:21.406 --> 00:32:23.408
And Kamala's saying,
or Elizabeth Warren,

00:32:23.408 --> 00:32:25.643 align:start size:81% position:19%
I think Kamala
said it too about,

00:32:25.643 --> 00:32:28.046
black transgender women are
the backbone of the economy.

00:32:28.046 --> 00:32:29.514
I mean, like really crazy stuff

00:32:29.514 --> 00:32:31.983
that no one's against
transgender people.

00:32:31.983 --> 00:32:35.720
But just how this has become
such a part of the zeitgeists.

00:32:35.720 --> 00:32:37.989
Like, this is like
a bellwether thing

00:32:37.989 --> 00:32:40.358
where you either accept
it or you're a dissident,

00:32:40.358 --> 00:32:41.459
you're a bad guy.

00:32:42.427 --> 00:32:43.528
- Yeah, it really has.

00:32:43.528 --> 00:32:44.762
You know, it's so interesting,

00:32:44.762 --> 00:32:46.531
when I first wrote a
proposal for my agent,

00:32:46.531 --> 00:32:47.765
it was actually gonna be

00:32:47.765 --> 00:32:49.267 align:start size:84% position:16%
on a contemporary
book about feminism.

00:32:49.267 --> 00:32:52.236 align:start size:97% position:3%
I had written one article
about this whole sudden spike

00:32:52.236 --> 00:32:54.872 align:start size:97% position:3%
in teenage girls
identifying as trans thing.

00:32:54.872 --> 00:32:57.141 align:start size:88% position:13%
But it certainly wasn't
a passion of mine

00:32:57.141 --> 00:32:59.777
and I wasn't intending
to turn it into a book.

00:32:59.777 --> 00:33:01.212
And my agent said to me,

00:33:01.212 --> 00:33:03.081
listen, that article you wrote

00:33:03.081 --> 00:33:05.984
seems to have gotten
a lot of attention.

00:33:05.984 --> 00:33:08.252 align:start size:97% position:3%
And frankly, if what
you're really interested in

00:33:08.252 --> 00:33:10.388
is how young women
today are doing,

00:33:10.388 --> 00:33:12.924 align:start size:88% position:13%
it seems to be a really
good way to explore

00:33:12.924 --> 00:33:14.859
all the other issues
you're interested in

00:33:14.859 --> 00:33:18.629 align:start size:97% position:3%
like free speech and how
young women are fairing today.

00:33:18.629 --> 00:33:23.634
So it did end up being
sort of incredible lens

00:33:24.802 --> 00:33:26.070
for looking at so many
aspects of the culture.

00:33:26.070 --> 00:33:28.806
So I guess that's
why it seems to be

00:33:28.806 --> 00:33:31.209
at the nexus of a lot
of different things.

00:33:31.209 --> 00:33:33.077
- Yeah, well, that's why
it's so fascinating to me

00:33:33.077 --> 00:33:35.380
because over the years I've
interviewed a lot of people

00:33:35.380 --> 00:33:39.317
who suddenly find themselves
in the thick of the battle

00:33:39.317 --> 00:33:41.219
without really wanting in on it.

00:33:41.219 --> 00:33:43.121 align:start size:97% position:3%
They were just sort of
interested in something else.

00:33:43.121 --> 00:33:45.223
And next thing, you know,
the battle comes to them.

00:33:45.223 --> 00:33:46.691
And even though I
hadn't, you know,

00:33:46.691 --> 00:33:47.959
this is the first time

00:33:47.959 --> 00:33:49.160
that we're actually
speaking one-on-one,

00:33:49.160 --> 00:33:50.928
when I saw the Target
thing, I was like,

00:33:50.928 --> 00:33:52.430
I'm gonna go out on a limb

00:33:52.430 --> 00:33:55.166 align:start size:97% position:3%
and guess that Abigail is
probably not that combative,

00:33:55.166 --> 00:33:58.569
probably didn't really want
all of this extra attention

00:33:58.569 --> 00:34:00.071
and everything else.

00:34:00.071 --> 00:34:01.672
So what has it been like
for you to be a dissident

00:34:01.672 --> 00:34:05.376
in something that is
so hard to talk about?

00:34:05.376 --> 00:34:09.547
- You know, I wouldn't have
written this book, kind of,

00:34:09.547 --> 00:34:11.349
if I didn't think a few things,

00:34:11.349 --> 00:34:12.984 align:start size:84% position:16%
if I didn't think what
was going on today

00:34:12.984 --> 00:34:14.752
is kind of madness.

00:34:14.752 --> 00:34:17.488
I do believe we're gonna look
back on this time and say,

00:34:17.488 --> 00:34:18.990
what were we doing?

00:34:18.990 --> 00:34:20.324
I mean, why were we letting

00:34:21.459 --> 00:34:24.362 align:start size:84% position:16%
very upset teenagers
in a lot of pain

00:34:24.362 --> 00:34:26.798 align:start size:84% position:16%
immediately
medically transition,

00:34:26.798 --> 00:34:30.568
and risk there fertility and
future sexual dysfunction?

00:34:30.568 --> 00:34:32.670
So I think that's what
the high court in England

00:34:32.670 --> 00:34:33.838
just looked at last week.

00:34:33.838 --> 00:34:35.339
It was a major case.

00:34:35.339 --> 00:34:37.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course the media in the
U.S. tried to ignore it

00:34:37.708 --> 00:34:39.177
and mostly did.

00:34:39.177 --> 00:34:41.646 align:start size:97% position:3%
But it was a huge case,
this is a neutral tribunal.

00:34:41.646 --> 00:34:43.514
And they looked at the
exact same protocols

00:34:43.514 --> 00:34:46.150
we have in place today
and they were horrified.

00:34:46.150 --> 00:34:47.618 align:start size:84% position:16%
They basically
said, why aren't...

00:34:47.618 --> 00:34:51.989 align:start position:0%
You know, these young kids can't
give informed consent at 15

00:34:53.157 --> 00:34:54.225 align:start size:84% position:16%
to eliminating their
future fertility.

00:34:54.225 --> 00:34:55.593
What are we doing?

00:34:55.593 --> 00:34:57.528 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, but what about
for you personally,

00:34:57.528 --> 00:35:00.098
just like going through the
headaches of all of this.

00:35:00.098 --> 00:35:03.267 align:start size:97% position:3%
And you were on Joe Rogan
and then the Spotify people,

00:35:03.267 --> 00:35:05.069 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, some
employees at Spotify

00:35:05.069 --> 00:35:06.971
basically wanted to
kick him off Spotify.

00:35:06.971 --> 00:35:08.673
Fortunately, that didn't happen.

00:35:08.673 --> 00:35:10.541
Everyone heard what
happened with Target,

00:35:10.541 --> 00:35:11.576
but you're back into Target.

00:35:11.576 --> 00:35:13.111
I mean, just for you personally,

00:35:13.111 --> 00:35:15.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
as someone that, you
know, you're now out there

00:35:15.046 --> 00:35:17.281
and you live in L.A.,
I mean, you're here

00:35:17.281 --> 00:35:20.084
in this weird town, you know?

00:35:20.084 --> 00:35:21.619
Just the personal cost.
- You know what's funny?

00:35:21.619 --> 00:35:23.121
When I wrote the book,

00:35:23.121 --> 00:35:25.923
I actually worried that it
would be completely ignored.

00:35:25.923 --> 00:35:27.525
(laughing)

00:35:27.525 --> 00:35:28.626
- Little did you know.

00:35:30.495 --> 00:35:33.231
- I was surprised a little bit.

00:35:33.231 --> 00:35:34.632
But I had seen...

00:35:34.632 --> 00:35:36.467 align:start size:97% position:3%
I wasn't completely surprised
and I'll tell you why.

00:35:36.467 --> 00:35:39.704 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because I had watched every
scientist who has ever,

00:35:39.704 --> 00:35:41.672 align:start size:88% position:13%
and many of them I
interviewed in the book,

00:35:41.672 --> 00:35:45.610 align:start size:97% position:3%
who has ever come out
against affirmative therapy,

00:35:45.610 --> 00:35:46.711
who has ever come out and said,

00:35:46.711 --> 00:35:48.246
hold on, what's going on?

00:35:48.246 --> 00:35:50.982
Does seems to have a
lot of peer influence.

00:35:50.982 --> 00:35:54.018
Or have said, this isn't real
therapy, there's no oversight.

00:35:54.018 --> 00:35:56.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every scientist who's done
that has been canceled.

00:35:56.888 --> 00:35:59.423 align:start size:84% position:16%
And sometimes they've
lost their jobs.

00:35:59.423 --> 00:36:01.592 align:start size:97% position:3%
And very often they've been
really caught off guard

00:36:01.592 --> 00:36:04.595 align:start size:88% position:13%
by the vitriol and
the, frankly, bad faith

00:36:04.595 --> 00:36:06.063
on the opposite side.

00:36:06.063 --> 00:36:08.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I at least had the
benefit of their example.

00:36:08.866 --> 00:36:12.770
And I was a little bit
more prepared for that.

00:36:12.770 --> 00:36:15.306
- Right, has it cost you, do
you think, professionally?

00:36:15.306 --> 00:36:17.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, the book is
obviously doing well now.

00:36:17.742 --> 00:36:20.244 align:start size:84% position:16%
But do you think this
will ultimately close
some other doors

00:36:20.244 --> 00:36:23.147
that you may not
even know about?

00:36:23.147 --> 00:36:25.883
- I'm sure, I mean you
know, it's a question...

00:36:25.883 --> 00:36:28.719 align:start size:97% position:3%
I do believe that we're
gonna look back on this age.

00:36:28.719 --> 00:36:31.923
I mean look, you
know, in England

00:36:31.923 --> 00:36:33.958
where they have the exact
same medical protocols

00:36:33.958 --> 00:36:37.428
and the exact same spike
among adolescent girls

00:36:37.428 --> 00:36:39.664 align:start size:88% position:13%
'cause they have the
same social media we do,

00:36:42.867 --> 00:36:46.504
The Economist and
The Times of London

00:36:46.504 --> 00:36:51.309
both just named my book to a
best books list for the year.

00:36:51.309 --> 00:36:54.312
So even though the legacy
media in the United States

00:36:54.312 --> 00:36:56.414
completely ignored my book,

00:36:56.414 --> 00:37:00.885
in England, their media seems
to have found it worthwhile.

00:37:00.885 --> 00:37:03.054
So, you know, I'm hoping

00:37:03.054 --> 00:37:05.623 align:start size:81% position:19%
the sanity at some
point prevails.

00:37:05.623 --> 00:37:07.425
- Yeah, you know, I'm wondering,

00:37:07.425 --> 00:37:09.060
I wonder if there's
any numbers on this.

00:37:09.060 --> 00:37:10.328 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm sure someone
could figure it out.

00:37:10.328 --> 00:37:12.063
But I find whenever
I just suddenly get

00:37:12.063 --> 00:37:14.665
like 1000 hate tweets in a row,

00:37:14.665 --> 00:37:16.467
almost every single one of them,

00:37:16.467 --> 00:37:18.970
if I look at the bio of
the people that send it,

00:37:18.970 --> 00:37:20.571
has gender pronouns in there.

00:37:20.571 --> 00:37:22.473
And I always think it's so
interesting that, you know,

00:37:22.473 --> 00:37:26.077 align:start position:0%
the people that I suppose
purport to be the most tolerant,

00:37:26.077 --> 00:37:27.612
the most diverse, the most open,

00:37:27.612 --> 00:37:31.048
that they're the ones that are
often sending the most anger.

00:37:31.048 --> 00:37:32.984
So I can only imagine

00:37:32.984 --> 00:37:35.987
what you are opening up
your Twitter to find.

00:37:35.987 --> 00:37:37.421
- From the tolerant people.

00:37:37.421 --> 00:37:40.791 align:start position:0%
- (laughs) Yeah, you can imagine
the sort of threats I get.

00:37:40.791 --> 00:37:42.860
But I would just
say that, you know,

00:37:42.860 --> 00:37:46.030 align:start size:84% position:16%
look, I know a
lot of transgender
adults at this point.

00:37:46.030 --> 00:37:49.033
And then I try to say
this in every interview

00:37:49.033 --> 00:37:50.434
because it's really true.

00:37:50.434 --> 00:37:53.371
The crazy woke activists
do not speak for them.

00:37:53.371 --> 00:37:55.506 align:start size:84% position:16%
They don't represent
these crazies.

00:37:55.506 --> 00:37:58.309 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they are not represented
by these crazies.

00:37:58.309 --> 00:38:00.111 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I have to say,
transgender people I've met

00:38:00.111 --> 00:38:02.446 align:start size:84% position:16%
are some of the
loveliest most sober

00:38:02.446 --> 00:38:05.583 align:start size:97% position:3%
and really insightful
people I've gotten to know.

00:38:05.583 --> 00:38:07.752
So these woke activists,

00:38:07.752 --> 00:38:10.488
they are the same people
leading black lives matter

00:38:10.488 --> 00:38:13.357 align:start size:84% position:16%
and every other
extreme group today.

00:38:13.357 --> 00:38:16.260 align:start size:88% position:13%
And they don't represent
transgender people.

00:38:16.260 --> 00:38:17.728
Certainly the ones I've-

00:38:17.728 --> 00:38:18.863
- Actually, I kind of
want it to get there.

00:38:18.863 --> 00:38:19.997
Can you talk a little bit

00:38:19.997 --> 00:38:22.233 align:start size:88% position:13%
about the intersectional
nature of this?

00:38:22.233 --> 00:38:24.568
How it went from
